closest-possible: same parse-then-interpret structure with loops handled recursively and the same checksum (warmup results discarded from the checksum, as Crystal does). Crystal builds nested ::Array(Op) loop bodies; this port uses a flat op list where each loop op stores the index just past its body, and the body is executed recursively over that range (a nested op-tree variant was not tried; the flat form keeps the Op struct fixed-size for stage 0). Loop iterations are capped by STEP_LIMIT. The tape is a fixed 30000-cell int array wrapped with % 256 instead of Crystal's growable UInt8 tape (next-lang stage 0 rejects (byte) casts, and fixed arrays cannot grow; these programs never leave cells 0..30000). Parse and run happen per call, as in Crystal. Prep mode prints the warmup-accumulated sink.
